                    {
                        "sense_id": "b60775fd-da68-3bdf-974d-c9eb50e81211",
                        "entry_id": "ff40585f-d8f4-3dff-a91c-622e127075bb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Serving to emphasize the certainty or truth of a statement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bcb7021b-337f-4323-8fbd-2bb638963ad2",
                                "sense_id": "b60775fd-da68-3bdf-974d-c9eb50e81211",
                                "text": "Further, it is strongly possible that the emphatic or asseverative lamed is etymologically distinct from the preposition, though the Masoretes do not distinguish the two."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8660d74-8164-40f5-b022-97b29d7f3871",
                                "sense_id": "b60775fd-da68-3bdf-974d-c9eb50e81211",
                                "text": "A prosthetic 'aleph was added in Hebrew […] and this gave a graphemic distinction between the negative and the asseverative, but the asseverative nevertheless eventually disappeared in Hebrew and other Canaanite dialects."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9264e07-1c7c-417c-9ba5-da0cb6595cbd",
                                "sense_id": "b60775fd-da68-3bdf-974d-c9eb50e81211",
                                "text": "Delimiting the forms which belong to the asseverative paradigm can be achieved only for some of the forms based on morphological criteria alone."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
